[V:LH] z2 [F,,F,]2 [A,,A,]2 | [F,,F,]2 [F,A,C]2 [F,A,C]2 | z2 [E,,E,]2 [C,,C,]2 | [G,,G,]2 [E,G,C]2 [E,G,C]2 | [D,,D,]2 [D,F,A,]2 [E,,E,]2 | [F,,F,]2 [D,,D,]2 [G,,G,]2 |
% ? p1 s1 b4: RH beat 3 lowest head sits between E4 and D4 without ledger; read as E ([EGB] = C7)
% ok Claude (druhé čítanie) 2026-11-20: p1 s1 b6: RH chords drawn loosely around a misplaced ledger; read as [B,DF] / [B,DG]; LH beat 1 low note read as F2 (octave of F3), drawn near D2 — Read against the single ledger the writer drew (meant as the middle-C ledger), the heads come out Bb-D-F and Bb-D-G. That fits the bass (F, D, G octaves) and the bar-by-bar descent of parallel chords from bar 4. The low bass F is the writer's usual low F drawn at D height.
% p1 s2
[V:RH] [C-FA]6 | [CFA]6 | FF [CF]2 [FA]2 | [FAc]6 | EE [CE]2 [EG]2 |
[V:LH] [F,,F,]2 [C,,C,]2 [A,,,A,,]2 | [F,,,F,,]2 [A,,,A,,]2 [C,,C,]2 | z2 [C,F,]2 [F,A,]2 | [F,,F,]2 [F,A,C]2 [F,A,C]2 | z2 [E,,E,]2 [C,,C,]2 |
% ok Claude (druhé čítanie) 2026-11-20: p1 s2 b1-2: arc under the RH bottom C read as a tie; ledger-line octaves in LH counted from compressed ledgers — The arc joins the same note, the bottom C, in both bars, so it is a tie. Counting the ledgers, every LH pair is an octave of F, C or A; all are F-chord notes.
% p1 s3
[V:RH] [EGc]4 [EB]2 | [CEA]4 [EG]2 | [G,B,D]4 [G,CE]2 | [A,CF]6- | [A,CF]2 z4 | C2 [CF]2 [FA]2 |
[V:LH] [G,,G,]2 [E,,E,]2 [C,,C,]2 | [C,,C,]2 [E,,E,]2 [G,,G,]2 | [G,,,G,,]2 [B,,,B,,]2 [C,,C,]2 | [F,,C,F,]6 | [F,,C,F,]2 z4 | [F,,F,]2 [A,C]2 [A,C]2 |
% ok Claude (druhé čítanie) 2026-11-20: p1 s3 b2: RH top head is in the A4 space (C6 over C arpeggio); G4 would be the plain C chord — The top head sits squarely in the A space, a full step above the G line. A falling to G on beat 3 is an ordinary added-sixth figure.
% ok Claude (druhé čítanie) 2026-11-20: p1 s3 b3: LH beat 2 lower head sits on the A1 ledger; read as B♭1 (octave of B♭2) — The low head is drawn one step high, but it is the octave below the clear Bb on the line, and a seventh (A under Bb) is not possible in this oom-pah bass. Bb is the only reading.
% p1 s4
[V:RH] [Fc]4 A2 | F4 D2 | E6 | C2 [CE]2 [CG]2 | [Ec]4 B2 |
